{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vnlcqazod5gmusdxa3u5jawpiltzdee7poe7abnlac7nlz6yhtra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **all four phases pass, one real bug found and fixed**.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | ✅ 10/10 C symbols exported by Rust `.so`; 0 missing; undefined = libc/loader only |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | ✅ 33 rows / 32 tests, seeded-random inputs (~10k calls) |\n| Binary stdout diff | N/A — no `add_executable`/`[[bin]]`; stdout compared at the FFI level instead |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | ✅ 17 rows + 3 generic-boundary tests, 21 tests |\n| All feature combinations | ✅ no `[features]` table → `release`/`dev` × default/`--no-default-features`, all green |\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n\n`checkshift`'s allocation-failure path was **missing from the Rust binary**. LLVM used its built-in knowledge that `malloc` returns non-null and deleted the `state == NULL` branch entirely — the `Error: Failed to allocate memory for state` string wasn't even in the `.so`, and the `-1` sentinel was unreachable. The C compiler keeps that branch, so with `malloc` interposed to fail the 12-byte request, C printed the diagnostic and returned `-1` while Rust dereferenced null.\n\nFix: wrapped the allocation in `core::hint::black_box` (`src/lib.rs:322`). Both libraries now produce identical output and `-1`.\n\n## Deliverables (in `translation/`)\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md` — Phase A artifacts, all rows checked off\n- `tests/common/mod.rs` — loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading` (no direct Rust calls), plus fd-1 stdout capture and a seeded SplitMix64 generator\n- `tests/phase_b_valid.rs` (32 tests), `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` (20), `tests/phase_c_malloc_fail.rs` (1, with a real `malloc` interposer)\n- `run_tests.sh` — builds C + Rust, diffs symbols, runs the full profile × feature matrix\n\n## Notes\n\n- Tests must run serially (`RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`, enforced by an assertion) since the harness redirects fd 1 process-wide; `run_tests.sh` sets it.\n- Non-vacuity confirmed by mutation testing: 5 injected Rust mutations (constant change, arithmetic→logical shift, removed `printf`, dropped checksum mask, `get_operation` off-by-one) were each caught, then reverted.\n- `c_src/` was not modified; only `c_src/build/` artifacts were generated."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3943,"cache_read_input_tokens":108129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3943,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b175d5f-493c-4765-a910-c44c15a2b978","uuid":"7ced619f-ce44-4771-b5f0-8de20e3c8615","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:45:44.971Z"}
